                <pb facs="0692" n="572" xml:id="pg572"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the King of Italy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >White House</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Majesty</hi>: I was gratified to receive your
                    telegram of the 30th ultimo, expressive of your appreciation of the presence of
                    the United States naval vessel <hi rendition="#italic">Minneapolis</hi> at the
                    Genoa fetes.</p>
                <p>It gave me great pleasure to manifest the cordial good will which this government
                    and people hold toward Your Majesty and the Italian people, by directing the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minneapolis</hi> to represent the United States on an
                    occasion to which Your Majesty’s presence gave national interest and
                    importance.</p>
                <p>Your good friend,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Theodore
                    Roosevelt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
